{
  "title": "Mag ik vrij nemen?",
  "goal": "Ask for permission and talk about ability, possibility, rules and obligations with kunnen, mogen and moeten.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "Mag ik vrij nemen?",
      "id": "3c3f2ff3-b470-447b-8a7f-04cd6bde0de8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Monday 7 December. Sofia wants to visit her family in Valencia at Christmas. She asks Karin about leave, then visits the pool on Wednesday. In this lesson you will choose between kunnen, mogen and moeten. Modal verbs are blue, infinitives are red, and the target modal forms are bold.",
      "id": "6ad84220-f4a8-4743-854d-07d824b0fcb7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: asking Karin",
      "id": "b4497d20-c456-4ede-9923-be8ccbe5ab3b"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Karin, mag ik vrij nemen van 21 december tot en met 31 december?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Karin",
            "text": "Dat mag. Je moet het wel in het systeem aanvragen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Dank je. Kan ik vrijdag thuiswerken?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Karin",
            "text": "Ja, dat kan. Op vrijdag mag je thuiswerken."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Moet ik acht dagen aanvragen?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Karin",
            "text": "Ja. Eerste kerstdag en tweede kerstdag zijn feestdagen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "En 1 januari is ook een feestdag."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Karin",
            "text": "Precies. Dan begin je op maandag 4 januari weer, toch?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "cfb56578-ec5a-40dc-9688-08e91de30bb0"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "vrij nemen",
              "meaning": "to take time off",
              "example": "Sofia neemt vrij van maandag 21 december tot en met donderdag 31 december.",
              "id": "47f7fb40-5b2a-44c9-90ee-2db31589986f"
            },
            {
              "term": "de vrije dag",
              "meaning": "day off",
              "forms": "de vrije dagen",
              "id": "6e30f2e6-d415-4e52-91b3-a8ab9f54388a"
            },
            {
              "term": "de kerstvakantie",
              "meaning": "Christmas holiday",
              "id": "855a093b-a545-4e48-a245-19993fabdf5e",
              "forms": "de kerstvakanties"
            },
            {
              "term": "de vakantie",
              "meaning": "holiday, vacation",
              "forms": "de vakanties",
              "id": "81993a35-925d-4df2-b8cf-c4d19fcf90a0"
            },
            {
              "term": "Kerstmis",
              "meaning": "Christmas",
              "id": "8dbae8cb-3e4a-48c8-922c-595ad0b75d7a"
            },
            {
              "term": "aanvragen",
              "meaning": "to request, apply for",
              "forms": "vraagt aan · vroeg aan · aangevraagd",
              "example": "Je moet het wel in het systeem aanvragen.",
              "note": "Separable verb: vraagt … aan.",
              "id": "17a7f96e-d4f2-43c1-b64d-84e62743bd9e"
            },
            {
              "term": "het systeem",
              "meaning": "system",
              "id": "18c615c7-ced5-465a-9874-3aab9d086e15"
            },
            {
              "term": "thuiswerken",
              "meaning": "to work from home",
              "forms": "werkt thuis · werkte thuis · thuisgewerkt",
              "example": "Op vrijdag mag je thuiswerken.",
              "id": "3741d2b4-93ef-4bbc-869c-5fa1ab612618"
            },
            {
              "term": "de feestdag",
              "meaning": "public holiday",
              "forms": "de feestdagen",
              "id": "58df27e0-e1ad-4446-b1aa-5246880ee7bc"
            },
            {
              "term": "tot en met",
              "meaning": "through, up to and including",
              "example": "Van 21 tot en met 31 december.",
              "id": "8ac43c19-c08a-4b8a-8aa4-673c8eabba10"
            },
            {
              "term": "eerste kerstdag",
              "meaning": "Christmas Day (25 December)",
              "id": "d2e0d4c2-afea-49bb-bb4a-e01fe083ce29"
            },
            {
              "term": "tweede kerstdag",
              "meaning": "Boxing Day (26 December)",
              "id": "cd152ee9-0b0b-48bb-9c91-84cbfcadeaff"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "e0049037-d97a-4854-bb95-2f55c20cf97b"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Three modal verbs",
      "id": "824dedec-f3cd-4bda-b3bf-65b06a655fed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A modal verb is conjugated. The other verb, if there is one, stays as an infinitive at the end. With ik, kunnen becomes kan, mogen becomes mag, and moeten becomes moet.",
      "id": "44ed2115-90f8-4b27-b9ba-a1205dd59be4"
    },
    {
      "type": "columnList",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "kunnen",
              "id": "87055fb0-62c3-44e4-9621-50988a0388b8"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": "can: ability or possibility",
              "id": "35def136-d61a-4d1d-b23d-5472583a9040"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                "Ik ",
                {
                  "text": "kan",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " zwemmen."
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "I can swim.",
                "note": "Ability."
              },
              "id": "cb6d0482-1d16-4d03-9c72-6837b27b5ff3"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                "Je ",
                {
                  "text": "kunt",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " op vrijdag thuiswerken."
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "You can work from home on Friday.",
                "note": "It is possible under the office rule."
              },
              "id": "5d9fd543-fd17-477b-8003-8d4c6e2e0056"
            }
          ],
          "id": "160686e6-d999-4a7b-b9c0-efce22fec29e"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "mogen",
              "id": "5e17fbcf-525b-4ce1-b3e3-982ac3c19f90"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": "may: permission; mogen niet means not allowed",
              "id": "b63b0ee7-66cf-46d3-b293-cd56d1945ece"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Mag",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " ik vrij nemen?"
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "May I take time off?",
                "note": "A polite request for permission."
              },
              "id": "df96ffc4-ab1c-46ba-8e2d-9b9b23ed0978"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                "Hier ",
                {
                  "text": "mag",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " je niet rennen."
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "You may not run here.",
                "note": "Mogen niet means prohibited."
              },
              "id": "fee44051-caef-4906-bdf7-1d508b4baf76"
            }
          ],
          "id": "283e61a3-5e70-4d09-a823-787908237ee3"
        },
        {
          "type": "column",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "props": {
                "level": 3
              },
              "content": "moeten",
              "id": "fcdb6752-2696-4597-8c81-ba3ceb23ec81"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": "must, have to: obligation",
              "id": "a591a2ae-230e-4e0b-8156-60a0a2bc4cf9"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                "Je ",
                {
                  "text": "moet",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " eerst douchen."
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "You must shower first.",
                "note": "A pool rule."
              },
              "id": "9c97d63c-f5dc-4131-aa63-116eb4f11c3d"
            },
            {
              "type": "example",
              "content": [
                "Sofia ",
                {
                  "text": "moet",
                  "styles": {
                    "bold": true,
                    "textColor": "blue"
                  }
                },
                " het in het systeem aanvragen."
              ],
              "props": {
                "translation": "Sofia has to request it in the system.",
                "note": "An obligation at work."
              },
              "id": "fb0f68c8-9db9-4f52-9a57-d3c11fe7cff2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "0d3c65c6-2045-4ddb-ba66-04f4429bc965"
        }
      ],
      "id": "a1802aaa-fdbc-4561-ac5e-798a17296979"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "kunnen = can / possible; mogen = may / permitted; moeten = must / required. Modal + subject + (other words) + infinitive at the end.",
      "id": "fc17385a-8031-4a54-8760-74323aee470e"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Daan ",
        {
          "text": "kan",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " vandaag niet ",
        {
          "text": "overwerken",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "red"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Daan can't work overtime today.",
        "note": "The infinitive stays at the end. Recycles overwerken from 20-a."
      },
      "id": "6a0023fb-ac16-44f1-b7bd-c133beb28151"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Ik ",
        {
          "text": "mag",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " hier naar binnen."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "I may go inside here.",
        "note": "Mogen can be followed by a direction without another infinitive."
      },
      "id": "810ffd8e-84ae-4537-939b-65c739ab3b77"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Dat ",
        {
          "text": "moet",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "That is required.",
        "note": "The modal can stand alone when the action is clear."
      },
      "id": "f612372e-0458-45c8-8f7a-3db0c16069db"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "hint",
        "icon": "lightbulb"
      },
      "content": "At work, Mag ik …? is a safe, polite way to ask permission. Kan ik …? asks whether something is possible.",
      "id": "fa85219c-8e6c-43dc-9c5b-9e5902d5104c"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Kan",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " ik op vrijdag thuiswerken?"
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Can I work from home on Friday?",
        "note": "This asks about possibility; Mag ik thuiswerken? asks for permission."
      },
      "id": "8e0fdd0d-6d48-4302-8410-06a1da636363"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Je moet niet rennen.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " usually means you shouldn't run. For a clear prohibition, say ",
        {
          "text": "Je mag niet rennen.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        ". Do not confuse it with moeten niet; that contrast comes in 23-b."
      ],
      "id": "c218d66d-5157-4402-a810-851b9a151e49"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "culture",
        "icon": "globe"
      },
      "content": "The Netherlands has two Christmas public holidays: eerste kerstdag (25 December) and tweede kerstdag (26 December). People arrange extra leave with their employer.",
      "id": "a38fd716-e3d6-40fa-a6fd-49c8db70a052"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Permission, possibility or obligation?",
      "id": "831a0ec4-6dba-4104-aeb8-be2de88bc1e7"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Ask permission: Mag ik …?",
      "id": "b4d81e4b-9009-4735-8dc3-27b4a334b1d8"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Ask if it is possible: Kan ik …?",
      "id": "7b0f5f06-a740-4bec-bc18-b05027c44037"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "State a rule: Je moet … / Je mag niet …",
      "id": "c7ff1dd9-3859-483e-a9d7-dd2391e200d4"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "The modal can stand alone: Dat mag. Dat kan niet. Dat moet.",
      "id": "91bea9a5-a82f-4af3-bd1b-e18ecde89ccd"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "At the pool:",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "Niet rennen. → Je mag niet rennen.",
          "id": "94e63ae4-efd9-45a8-89cc-c55d8437f218"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "Eerst douchen. → Je moet eerst douchen.",
          "id": "33002859-ceff-43bf-9834-3f56598142f5"
        }
      ],
      "id": "6aa3a0a4-7854-43d3-a112-7bf5751a3255"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Useful forms and signs",
      "id": "d1c3f612-8460-4a2c-b49d-4ab055c88799"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Op vrijdag ",
        {
          "text": "mag",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " je thuiswerken."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "You may work from home on Friday.",
        "note": "Permission."
      },
      "id": "25a8747c-a8f6-48af-a8d4-1ec1cd7c1387"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia ",
        {
          "text": "kan",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " goed ",
        {
          "text": "zwemmen",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "red"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia can swim well.",
        "note": "Ability; zwemmen is a known word from 19-a."
      },
      "id": "8df2f656-88e6-4a60-8bc0-64951913e910"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Je ",
        {
          "text": "moet",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " je ticket ",
        {
          "text": "aanvragen",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "red"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "You have to request your ticket.",
        "note": "A separable infinitive stays together at the end."
      },
      "id": "e8da7865-845d-4804-91b0-8f4f3c2198ab"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "het ticket",
              "meaning": "ticket",
              "forms": "de tickets",
              "id": "615166aa-8d54-4f3a-bcb7-7fc5ae1d9030",
              "example": "Je moet je ticket aanvragen."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "3a025f98-1cb5-48ef-b472-796775aef005"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Hier ",
        {
          "text": "mag",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " je niet ",
        {
          "text": "fietsen",
          "styles": {
            "textColor": "red"
          }
        },
        "."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "You are not allowed to cycle here.",
        "note": "Mogen niet gives a prohibition."
      },
      "id": "51863afe-90e5-4efb-892d-83dd03822f85"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Dat ",
        {
          "text": "kan",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " niet."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "That is not possible.",
        "note": "The context supplies the action."
      },
      "id": "d4958762-d14f-4193-ab3a-28bc6fa3b581"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "content": "A sign often uses a short infinitive: Niet rennen. In a full sentence, use mogen niet: Je mag hier niet rennen.",
      "id": "9cf1f314-aa4a-46b7-b023-cc96f9638ed9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Dutch pool rules often ask visitors to shower before swimming. The lifeguard is de badmeester. A kluis is a locker for your belongings.",
      "id": "8721bba3-0de0-415a-a703-71d7d1f3501d"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "de badmeester",
              "meaning": "lifeguard",
              "forms": "de badmeesters",
              "id": "2b6ebaeb-6452-4904-9fed-c99ea677ab8a"
            },
            {
              "term": "douchen",
              "meaning": "to shower",
              "forms": "doucht · douchte · gedoucht",
              "example": "Je moet eerst douchen.",
              "id": "ea550d34-ee60-48b8-85e0-d7f0672794ea"
            },
            {
              "term": "de kluis",
              "meaning": "locker",
              "forms": "de kluizen",
              "id": "619c23f8-a21f-4bcc-b227-8a15df4bc5f6"
            },
            {
              "term": "het diepe",
              "meaning": "the deep end of a swimming pool",
              "example": "Sofia kan in het diepe zwemmen.",
              "id": "00bc4cdc-e44b-489d-9275-1e89e5eb8f32"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "caf22170-c436-4b4b-b611-c8dd27b7ecf9"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: at the swimming pool",
      "id": "65a0bbdf-9dc0-424e-91f0-ba2b3ffcce21"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Badmeester",
            "text": "Goedemorgen. Je moet eerst douchen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Natuurlijk. Mag mijn tas hier staan?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Badmeester",
            "text": "Nee, dat mag niet. Je moet je tas in een kluis doen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Mag ik hier zwemmen?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Badmeester",
            "text": "Ja, dat mag. Maar je mag hier niet rennen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "En kan ik in het diepe zwemmen?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Badmeester",
            "text": "Dat kan. Je kunt goed zwemmen, toch?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik kan goed zwemmen. Dank u wel."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "edb8f979-50e8-4575-ad68-89c17b89ee55"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "bd4aa325-dd77-4937-aaa6-39f02da41621"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Practice",
      "id": "75c8dd9f-4bf9-4760-8edb-2a12b4ee497d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Choose the modal verb",
      "id": "967227c8-ef53-473a-a8ad-b3cae18739c8"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Fill in kunnen, mogen or moeten in the correct form. Decide: ability/possibility, permission, or obligation.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Ik … goed zwemmen.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "kan"
              ],
              "note": "Ability: I can swim."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "… ik vrij nemen?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Mag"
              ],
              "note": "Ask permission at work."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Je … het in het systeem aanvragen. (The rule says you have to.)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "moet"
              ],
              "note": "It is required."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Op vrijdag … je thuiswerken.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "kunt"
              ],
              "note": "It is possible under the office rule. Also fine: mag (permission)."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Hier … je niet rennen.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "mag"
              ],
              "note": "Mogen niet means not allowed."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Dat … niet. Het zwembad is dicht.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "kan"
              ],
              "note": "It is impossible; kan agrees with dat."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Je … eerst douchen.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "moet"
              ],
              "note": "A required pool rule."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "… ik mijn tas hier laten? (Ask permission.)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Mag"
              ],
              "note": "Ask permission."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia … naar Valencia vliegen. (She is able to.)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "kan"
              ],
              "note": "The parenthetical cues ability/possibility, so kunnen is intended."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Je … hier niet fietsen; het is een voetgangersgebied.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "mag"
              ],
              "note": "A prohibition."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij … maandag weer beginnen. (It is required.)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "moeten"
              ],
              "note": "A schedule or obligation."
            }
          ]
        }
