    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Summary",
      "id": "8dc5d37a-76d6-447c-884f-1b925cdc8d03"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "kunnen = can: ability or possibility. Dat kan niet = that is impossible.",
      "id": "5d006455-3537-4083-ad8e-5d9169ffef0c"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "mogen = may / be allowed. Mogen niet = not allowed.",
      "id": "4af3b03e-359d-42e0-b49c-1bb241e65d1a"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "moeten = must / have to: an obligation.",
      "id": "884c3992-a5f5-4c38-bc2f-7a1977a6afef"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Ask permission with Mag ik …? Ask about possibility with Kan ik …?",
      "id": "46b43f63-1bf0-4d23-ba6d-1a12d7dd1fdf"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "The modal is conjugated; an infinitive goes at the end: Je moet het aanvragen.",
      "id": "19d31a70-368d-4e8e-8071-19150c006238"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "A modal can stand alone: Dat mag. Dat kan. Dat moet.",
      "id": "07bf22af-4d07-4675-90f6-a086856d0348"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "2327c668-0bbd-4243-8b55-0a7b00d042aa"
